       SKILL.md, the page an AI agent reads to learn how to use the CLI
       (https://agentskills.io/specification). Keep it short: the format recommends under
       500 lines, and the per-command details live in references/. After rendering, rotini
       trims trailing whitespace, collapses blank-line runs and ends the page with a newline.

       DATA:
         .Name .Display .Summary .Description   the root command's name (the binary), the
                          name pages show, and its summary and description
         .SkillName       the skill's name, which is also its directory
         .SkillDescription  the frontmatter description: the root's summary, then the
                          feature's `description`
         .AllowedTools    Claude Code rules for the read-only leaf commands ("" for none)
         .Commands[]      the commands offered to agents, root first:
                          {.Invocation .Summary .Description .Aliases .Effects .Kind .Stability
                          .Deprecated .JSON .DryRun .Confirm .Examples .ExitStatus .Link}.
                          .Effects is the worst case over the command and its flags, in words,
                          and .Kind its kind (read, write, destructive, or "" when undeclared);
                          .JSON is what to add for JSON output; .DryRun and .Confirm are flags;
                          .ExitStatus rows are {.Code .Name .Summary .Retryable .DocsURL};
                          .Link is its reference page, "" when the markdown feature is off
         .Env[] .Config[] {.Name .Summary .Required .Secret .Commands} — what the commands read
                          from the environment and config files
         .JSON .Previews  some command has a JSON flag; some has a dry-run or confirm flag
       HELPERS: quote (a YAML/JSON string), join, upper, lower, title, trim, trimPrefix,
                trimSuffix, replace, indent, repeat, default, contains, hasPrefix, hasSuffix,
                first, last. */ -}}
